---
title: AdviseCare - Sequence Diagram SD-19 - Import Student Data
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor ADM as System Administrator
    participant W as Web App
    participant C as StudentDataController
    participant S as StudentDataService
    participant X as IExcelReader / ICsvReader
    participant K as IAttributeKeyService
    participant R as IGenericRepository
    participant DB as SQL Server
    ADM->>W: Upload file and map columns
    W->>C: POST /api/StudentData/import/preview
    C->>S: PreviewAsync(request)
    S->>X: Read header and first rows
    S-->>W: Header and sample rows
    W->>C: POST /api/StudentData/import {file, mapping}
    C->>S: CreateAsync(CreatorId, request)
    S->>X: Read all rows
    S->>R: Students (email, username, student code), data attributes, terms
    S->>S: Check every row (student, attribute, value type, term, valid-from), set aside rows of archived attributes
    alt any invalid row
        S-->>C: CreateStudentDataResponse (errors, nothing written)
    else all valid
        S->>K: EncryptValuesAsync(values) (a student's first value for an attribute creates and stages its key)
        K-->>S: encrypted payloads
        S->>R: PrepareCreate STUDENTDATA rows (status = original, provenanceNote = file + date)
        S->>R: PrepareCreate missing rows for enrolled students without a value
        S->>R: SaveAsync()
        R->>DB: INSERT ATTRIBUTEKEYS, STUDENTDATA (one transaction)
        S->>S: Log activity studentDataImported
        S-->>C: CreateStudentDataResponse (imported, missing, rejected rows)
    end
    C-->>W: 200 OK
